description: Coding conventions, naming, and how to change code safely
---

# Patterns and conventions

## General TypeScript/Nuxt

- Node >= 24.14, TypeScript (~5.9), Nuxt 4
- app/tsconfig.json and app/server/tsconfig.json extend Nuxt-generated configs; keep type imports/circular deps minimal
- Prefer small, focused modules; colocate tests under __tests__ near the code or in app/tests/

## API routes (Nitro/H3)

- File paths mirror URL paths (e.g., server/api/foo/bar.get.ts → GET /api/foo/bar)
- Method suffix: .get.ts, .post.ts, .patch.ts, .delete.ts
- Guarding:
  - Use app/server/middleware/auth.ts to require sessions (and server/lib/requireAdmin.ts for admin)
  - Use withErrorHandler.ts or handleApiError.ts to normalize errors
- Validation: use Zod schemas (app/schema/zod.ts or feature-specific files)
- Business logic: keep endpoints thin; delegate to app/server/services/* where possible
- Tests: add/update under app/server/api/__tests__ with Vitest

## Services

- Stateless functions where possible; pass explicit inputs
- Use server/clients/prismaClient.ts and redisClient.ts (do not instantiate Prisma directly)
- Shared helpers in server/lib/* (e.g., getPlaidClient, registerFuturePagination, handleApiError)

## Prisma and migrations

- Edit app/prisma/schema.prisma → run prisma migrate dev (local) → commit the migration directory
- Generate Prisma client before tests/build: pnpm --filter dineros-app exec prisma generate
- Governance: scripts/check-prisma-schema-governance.mjs validates schema constraints in CI
- Encrypted fields: annotated with /// @encrypted, /// @encryption:hash(...). Do not remove without a migration plan

## Queue/cron jobs

- Define queues in server/queues/*.ts, wired through server/clients/queuesClient.ts
- Schedule with app/server/cron/*.ts (nuxt-cron)
- Keep the job body idempotent and small; long-running tasks should chunk/paginate

## Frontend

- Use Pinia stores in app/stores; avoid global singletons outside Pinia
- Composables (app/composables) should be SSR-safe when used on server/route middleware
- Components follow PascalCase; props and emits typed; prefer small units
- Tailwind CSS with utility-first approach (see assets/css/main.css)

## Naming

- Branches: feat/*, fix/*, docs/* (see CONTRIBUTING.md)
- Files: kebab-case for modules, PascalCase for Vue SFCs
- Envs: DATABASE_URL lives in DB-specific secret; DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY/DB_DECRYPTION_KEY_* in a separate secret (see .deploy templates)

## Safe change guidelines

- Add API: create server/api path with method suffix, validate inputs, call service; add tests in server/api/__tests__
- Change schema: create migration, generate client, update services and tests; never edit migration_lock.toml
- Update forecast logic: prefer adding unit tests in server/services/forecast/__tests__ first; keep rateLimiter and ModernCacheService semantics intact
- Background job changes: ensure cron/queue naming remains consistent; update deployment docs if new env vars are required
- Security-sensitive code: never log secrets; use plaidApiError.ts and handleApiError.ts for sanitization; update .trufflehog-detectors.yaml if new secret patterns emerge
